{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01WAev9YXEAeCqpLBitUqYWp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/01-044-what-is-the-lost-in-the-middle-problem.md`** covering:\n\n- **Concept:** LLMs develop a U-shaped positional attention bias (primacy + recency) during RLHF/SFT — content in the middle of long prompts is systematically under-attended.\n- **Mechanism:** Liu et al. (2023) measured multi-doc QA accuracy dropping from ~70% (key doc at position 1) to ~45% (key doc at position 5–6 of 10). The RAGAS diagnostic: high `context_recall` + low `faithfulness` = lost-in-the-middle suspect.\n- **Mitigations table:** reduce K (less middle space), cross-encoder reranking (Cohere/MiniLM promote best chunk to position 1), reverse ordering, LLMLingua contextual compression, long-context models (Gemini 1.5 Pro).\n- **3 pitfalls:** the common mistake of increasing K (makes it worse), conflating it with hallucination, and prescribing \"put best chunk first\" without explaining reranking as the mechanism.\n- **Cross-links:** Q5 (context windows), Q43 (hallucination mitigations), Q14 in RAG category (reranking).\n\n**4 items remaining in Next:** Q45–Q48 + validate."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":58774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":342,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d108654e-b636-4a3e-b90a-945282f8533f","uuid":"9bdab660-5156-4a33-9bf4-17136a9bcf55"}
